{"affected":[{"modules":["Splunk Web"],"original_ranges":[{"lessThan":"8.1.7","status":"affected","version":"0","versionType":"custom"}],"product":"Splunk App for Stream","vendor":"Splunk"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-131301"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"datePublic":"2026-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"In Splunk App for Stream versions below 8.1.7, an unauthenticated user could cause Splunk App for Stream to reset its in-memory indexer cache.\nThe vulnerability exists because the Splunk Web handler accepts the cache-reset request without requiring a login.\nFor more information see Splunk Stream installation package overview (https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/collect-stream-data/install-and-configure-splunk-stream/8.0/introduction/splunk-stream-installation-package-overview) and Launch Splunk Web (https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.6/administer-splunk-enterprise-with-splunk-web/launch-splunk-web) in the Splunk documentation."}],"metrics":[{"cvssV3_1":{"baseScore":5.3,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","version":"3.1"},"format":"CVSS","scenarios":[{"lang":"en","value":"GENERAL"}]}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-862","description":"The software does not perform an authorization check when an actor attempts to access a resource or perform an action.","lang":"en","type":"cwe"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-19T19:56:46.662Z","orgId":"d1c1063e-7a18-46af-9102-31f8928bc633","shortName":"cisco"},"role":"cna","title":"Missing Authorization through Splunk Web in Splunk App for Stream"},{"affected_indices":[],"metrics":[{"other":{"content":{"id":"CVE-2026-131301","options":[{"Exploitation":"none"},{"Automatable":"yes"},{"Technical Impact":"partial"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:47:12.843125Z","version":"2.0.3"},"type":"ssvc"}}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-20T16:47:22.857Z","orgId":"134c704f-9b2